I'll go back to `WorkspaceNewRoomPage.tsx` and look at the `useEffect` hook that sets the `policyID`.

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
    if (policyID) {
        if (!workspaceOptions.some((opt) => opt.value === policyID)) {
            setPolicyID('');
        }
        return;
    }
    if (!!activePolicyID && workspaceOptions.some((opt) => opt.value === activePolicyID)) {
        setPolicyID(activePolicyID);
    } else {
        setPolicyID('');
    }
}, [activePolicyID, policyID, workspaceOptions]);
```

This code is setting the `policyID` to the `activePolicyID`. I need to change this to use the user's default workspace.

Based on the problem description, the user sets their default workspace in "old dot". This implies that the information is stored in the backend and should be available in the user's account information.

I'll search for "default policy" in the entire `src` directory to see if I can find any logic related to getting or setting a default policy.

